,"stop":"eos","text":"To find out what day of the week Kim's birthday fell on, we need to calculate the day of the week 200 days ago from today, which is Wednesday.\n\n1. **Understand the weekly cycle:** There are 7 days in a week. This means that every 7 days, the day of the week repeats.\n\n2. **Calculate the number of complete weeks in 200 days:** \n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of complete weeks} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{200}{7} \\right\\rfloor = 28 \\text{ weeks}\n   \\]\n   Multiplying the number of complete weeks by 7 gives us the total number of days in these weeks:\n   \\[\n   28 \\times 7 = 196 \\text{ days}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the remaining days:** Subtract the number of days in complete weeks from 200 days:\n   \\[\n   200 - 196 = 4 \\text{ days}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Count backwards from Wednesday:** We need to count backwards 4 days from Wednesday:\n   - 1 day before Wednesday is Tuesday.\n   - 2 days before Wednesday is Monday.\n   - 3 days before Wednesday is Sunday.\n   - 4 days before Wednesday is Saturday.\n\nTherefore, Kim's birthday was on a Saturday.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
